# Agent workflow (zombie-clicker)

Canonical doc: `docs/WORKFLOW.md` (also `AGENTS.md`).

## Roles

- **You (Cursor or Kimi)** = orchestrator: plans, Locked Decisions, review, **monitor**.
- **OpenCode + `ollama/qwen3.8-agent:27b`** = AFK executor (not the legacy `execute-plan-ollama.mjs`).
- **Orca** = optional runtime for visible terminals.

## When user asks to monitor (not build)

1. Inspect Orca terminal / diffs / tests.
2. Unblock infra/prompt/config; relaunch OpenCode.
3. Do **not** implement the feature yourself unless explicitly asked to code.

## When user asks for a feature / non-trivial fix

1. Prefer an AFK-safe plan under `docs/superpowers/plans/`.
2. Tell them how to launch OpenCode (see `docs/WORKFLOW.md`).
3. Do not re-implement the whole plan in parallel while OpenCode owns those files.

## Launch (executor)

```powershell
opencode run -m ollama/qwen3.8-agent:27b --auto --title "task-N" "Ejecutá SOLO Task N del plan <path>. Locked Decisions. Sin preguntas. Al final: node tests/logic.test.js"
```

Project config: `opencode.json` (Ollama provider + default model).

## Game constraints

- Vanilla HTML/CSS/JS only
- `game.js` = logic; `ui.js` = DOM; `cloud.js` = optional Supabase; `style.css` = look; `index.html` = structure
- No own backend; optional cloud save via Supabase CDN
- Run `node tests/logic.test.js` after logic/save changes
- Spanish UI copy
